# Real provider credentials. apps/.env-example is the template that IS
# committed; apps/.env is your working copy and must never be.
#
# The name matters: internal/adkenv walks up from the working directory
# looking for exactly "apps/.env", so this is the path a learner creates the
# moment they follow the README.
apps/.env

# The standalone agentgateway demo keeps its own env file.
demo/1_ai-gateway/.env

# `go build ./<dir>/` writes the binary into the CURRENT directory, named after
# the target dir. Building a lab from the repo root therefore drops an 80+ MB
# executable at the root, named "labs" — which is a directory in this tree.
/labs

# go build in a single-package dir writes the binary next to main.go
demo/1_ai-gateway/mock-llm/mock-llm

# `make build` / `make verify` in demo/adk-quickstart writes binaries here
demo/adk-quickstart/bin/
